        "id": "volskaya-foundry",
        "name": "Volskaya Foundry"
      }
    ],
    "explanation": "Having a well-rounded Ability set, E.T.C. works well on most Maps but performs better where he can flank—to Face Melt and then Powerslide as a safe engage—or fight near choke points—where he can easily hit enemy Heroes with Powerslide and his Heroic Abilities.\n\nBattlefield of Eternity is particularly interesting for E.T.C. because he can knockback and Stun enemy Heroes right below the allied Immortal to make it impossible for them to dodge his Abilities.\n\nWhile it is not necessarily a huge problem depending on the rest of your draft, E.T.C. is not that good for Maps where the Objective takes extremely long to be secured because, even if he has some self-sustain, he will struggle to be alive for long due to his below-average durability."
  },
